(Northwind Solar - Installation Handbook) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 1: Overview) Tj
T*
(The Northwind NS-400 is a residential rooftop solar array rated at) Tj
T*
(400 watts per panel. A standard household installation uses twelve) Tj
T*
(panels for a combined output of 4.8 kilowatts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 2: Site Requirements) Tj
T*
(Panels require a south-facing roof with a pitch between 15 and 40) Tj
T*
(degrees. The mounting rail must be anchored into rafters, never into) Tj
T*
(sheathing alone. Minimum clearance from any roof edge is 300 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 3: Electrical) Tj
T*
(Each string connects to the NS-Link inverter, which supports a maximum) Tj
T*
(of sixteen panels. The inverter must be installed indoors, within three) Tj
T*
(metres of the main consumer unit.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
<< /Length 881 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 750 Td
16 TL
(Northwind Solar - Installation Handbook \(page 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 4: Warranty) Tj
T*
(Panels carry a 25-year performance warranty guaranteeing at least 85) Tj
T*
(percent of rated output at year 25. The NS-Link inverter carries a) Tj
T*
(separate 10-year warranty. Labour is covered for the first 2 years.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 5: Maintenance) Tj
T*
(Rinse panels with clean water twice per year. Do not use detergents or) Tj
T*
(abrasive brushes, as these void the performance warranty. Inspect the) Tj
T*
(mounting bolts annually and torque them to 18 newton metres.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Section 6: Support) Tj
T*
(Registered installers may contact technical support for diagnostics.) Tj
T*
(Fault code E-14 indicates a string voltage mismatch and usually means) Tj
T*
(one panel in the string has been shaded or wired in reverse.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
